{"id":"43ae8fb2a07f84ab","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-coercive.md","title":"Coercive","display":"df-coercive — Coercive","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-coercive","aliases":["58-df-coercive","Coercive"],"display":"df-coercive — Coercive","depends_on":["[[../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-coercive"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-coercive</span><span>Coercive</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-coercive — Coercive"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"bdbbe5a00af04978\" href=\"?note=bdbbe5a00af04978\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md\">../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\">\\(\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\)</span> (scalar field)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(V,+_V,\\cdot_V,\\|\\cdot\\|_V)\">\\((V,+_V,\\cdot_V,\\|\\cdot\\|_V)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(H,+_H,\\cdot_H,\\|\\cdot\\|_H)\">\\((H,+_H,\\cdot_H,\\|\\cdot\\|_H)\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb K\">\\(\\mathbb K\\)</span>-normed spaces, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bdbbe5a00af04978\" href=\"?note=bdbbe5a00af04978\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md\">../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S\\)</span> (normed-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bdbbe5a00af04978\" href=\"?note=bdbbe5a00af04978\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md\">../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\\in\\mathbb K^{V\\times V}\">\\(a\\in\\mathbb K^{V\\times V}\\)</span> (bilinear form when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb K=\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb K=\\mathbb R\\)</span> and sesquilinear form when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb K=\\mathbb C\">\\(\\mathbb K=\\mathbb C\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Coercive}_S(a,V,\\mathbb K)\">\\(\\mathrm{Coercive}_S(a,V,\\mathbb K)\\)</span> (coercivity predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SemiCoercive}_S(a,V,H,\\mathbb K)\">\\(\\mathrm{SemiCoercive}_S(a,V,H,\\mathbb K)\\)</span> (Gårding-type semi-coercivity predicate)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}coercive} \\vdash \\mathrm{Coercive}_S(a,V,\\mathbb K) \\leftrightarrow \\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(V,\\mathbb K,+_V,\\cdot_V,\\|\\cdot\\|_V)\\land a\\in\\mathbb K^{V\\times V}\\land\\forall u,v,w\\in V\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathbb K\\;\\bigl(a(\\alpha u+v,w)=\\alpha a(u,w)+a(v,w)\\land a(u,\\alpha v+w)=\\overline\\alpha a(u,v)+a(u,w)\\bigr)\\land\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall v\\in V\\;(\\operatorname{Re}a(v,v)\\geq c\\|v\\|_V^2)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}coercive} \\vdash \\mathrm{Coercive}_S(a,V,\\mathbb K) \\leftrightarrow \\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(V,\\mathbb K,+_V,\\cdot_V,\\|\\cdot\\|_V)\\land a\\in\\mathbb K^{V\\times V}\\land\\forall u,v,w\\in V\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathbb K\\;\\bigl(a(\\alpha u+v,w)=\\alpha a(u,w)+a(v,w)\\land a(u,\\alpha v+w)=\\overline\\alpha a(u,v)+a(u,w)\\bigr)\\land\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall v\\in V\\;(\\operatorname{Re}a(v,v)\\geq c\\|v\\|_V^2)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}coercive\\text{-}semi} \\vdash \\mathrm{SemiCoercive}_S(a,V,H,\\mathbb K) \\leftrightarrow \\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(V,\\mathbb K,+_V,\\cdot_V,\\|\\cdot\\|_V)\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(H,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\cdot_H,\\|\\cdot\\|_H)\\land V\\subseteq H\\land\\exists C_0\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall v\\in V\\;(\\|v\\|_H\\leq C_0\\|v\\|_V)\\land a\\in\\mathbb K^{V\\times V}\\land\\forall u,v,w\\in V\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathbb K\\;\\bigl(a(\\alpha u+v,w)=\\alpha a(u,w)+a(v,w)\\land a(u,\\alpha v+w)=\\overline\\alpha a(u,v)+a(u,w)\\bigr)\\land\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\forall v\\in V\\;(\\operatorname{Re}a(v,v)\\geq c\\|v\\|_V^2-C\\|v\\|_H^2)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}coercive\\text{-}semi} \\vdash \\mathrm{SemiCoercive}_S(a,V,H,\\mathbb K) \\leftrightarrow \\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(V,\\mathbb K,+_V,\\cdot_V,\\|\\cdot\\|_V)\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(H,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\cdot_H,\\|\\cdot\\|_H)\\land V\\subseteq H\\land\\exists C_0\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall v\\in V\\;(\\|v\\|_H\\leq C_0\\|v\\|_V)\\land a\\in\\mathbb K^{V\\times V}\\land\\forall u,v,w\\in V\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathbb K\\;\\bigl(a(\\alpha u+v,w)=\\alpha a(u,w)+a(v,w)\\land a(u,\\alpha v+w)=\\overline\\alpha a(u,v)+a(u,w)\\bigr)\\land\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\forall v\\in V\\;(\\operatorname{Re}a(v,v)\\geq c\\|v\\|_V^2-C\\|v\\|_H^2)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Coercivity is a lower bound on the real part of the quadratic value of a real bilinear or complex sesquilinear form.</li>\n<li>Unique solvability is supplied by the Lax--Milgram theorem only after boundedness/continuity and completeness assumptions are added.</li>\n<li>A Gårding inequality allows a lower-order <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span>-norm defect, as recorded by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SemiCoercive}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SemiCoercive}_S\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Poincaré: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int|\\nabla u|^2 \\geq c\\|u\\|_{H^1}^2\">\\(\\int|\\nabla u|^2 \\geq c\\|u\\|_{H^1}^2\\)</span> for appropriate domains</li>\n<li>Legendre form: matrix <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Re}(v^* A v) \\geq c\\|v\\|^2\">\\(\\operatorname{Re}(v^* A v) \\geq c\\|v\\|^2\\)</span>; strong ellipticity</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Evans, Partial Differential Equations</li>\n<li>Brezis, Functional Analysis, Sobolev Spaces and PDEs</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"bdbbe5a00af04978","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"bdbbe5a00af04978","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$(V,+_V,\\cdot_V,\\|\\cdot\\|_V)$ and $(H,+_H,\\cdot_H,\\|\\cdot\\|_H)$ ($\\mathbb K$-normed spaces, see [[../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"bdbbe5a00af04978","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S$ (normed-space pred